+# PDFCraft 0.22.0 — Font Editor V1 (unofficial source revision)
+
+Base: user-supplied PDFCraft v0.22.0 archive, commit ac140f809d554981a5276d748e6193fcf4d4bdfa.
+This is a source revision, not a compiled or signed release. No upstream version number or dependencies were changed.
+
+## Changes
+- Edit a PDF sidebar: Document fonts section is visible before selecting existing text. Import font and Installed fonts are direct actions.
+- Format text: dedicated import/installed-font actions alongside the existing font dropdown. The existing installed-font discovery, search and family grouping are reused.
+- TTF/OTF: register on the current PDF page. When a specific paragraph initiated the picker, apply to that paragraph only if it remains open. If it is no longer open, register without rewriting text. The existing document/generation guard remains in place.
+- Explicitly report if registration succeeded but the font catalogue cannot list the face for immediate application.
+- A pending resource change counts as an edit; a caret-only (empty) range applies the font to the whole paragraph.
+- Existing font validator, Unicode embedding, resource selection, save and undo mechanisms retained. No font binaries or dependencies were added.
+
+## Scope and limitations
+- Custom font support is for existing editable PDF text. Add Text uses the existing standard-family renderer; custom Add Text is not implemented in V1. The UI explicitly reports this limitation.
+- Import is per page, not a persistent application font library; use the dropdown for registered faces on that page. Imports and text rewrites are separate undo steps.
+- Only static standalone fonts satisfying upstream validation, including its open-licence and embedding policy. No bypass of licence restrictions; font collections and variable fonts are not supported.
+- Existing source paragraph rewrite restrictions, text overflow, glyph coverage, and bounded font catalogue remain applicable. Existing font resources are not a permanent cross-document library.
+- The picker guards the originating document, generation, page and paragraph index. It does not freeze the original text selection range if a user changes that selection in the same open paragraph.
+- No installer, portable executable, binary or runtime validation was produced here. Rust/Cargo is unavailable in the development container. The new tests are written but unexecuted. The changes may require corrections after compilation.
+
+## Windows build
+Use Windows 10/11 x64, Rust 1.95 or newer (MSVC toolchain), Visual Studio Build Tools with Desktop development with C++, Windows SDK, Git, and network access to fetch the pinned dependencies. Follow upstream docs/development.md for optional build assets.
+
+Open PowerShell at the extracted repository root. To build the GUI:
+
+```powershell
+rustup target add x86_64-pc-windows-msvc
+cargo build --locked --release -p pdfcraft --target x86_64-pc-windows-msvc
+```
+
+The executable should be at `target\x86_64-pc-windows-msvc\release\pdfcraft.exe` after a successful build. The supplied `BUILD-FONT-EDITOR.ps1` runs that build; use `-RunTests` to run the text-editor library tests first. Do not replace your installed application until tests pass. Keep backups of PDFs and test using Save As.
+
+For official-style Windows packaging, see docs/releasing.md and packaging/windows/package.ps1. That process needs the additional WiX v5, OCR assets, optional font notices and other upstream prerequisites. The resulting local artifacts will not be official or signed unless separately configured with authorized signing credentials.
+
+## QC acceptance (not run)
+1. Open a copy of a PDF containing selectable text. Open Edit a PDF; confirm Document fonts is visible before choosing a paragraph.
+2. Import an eligible static `.ttf` (e.g. a licensed Inter face). Confirm the existing page text is unchanged until you explicitly apply the face.
+3. Click an existing paragraph and select the face from Format text. Verify displayed typeface, point size, text content, and baseline. Save As, reopen in PdfCraft and an independent reader, and check text selection/search.
+4. Repeat by using the direct Import font button while an existing paragraph is selected. Confirm font applies to that paragraph or its selected range. Test Installed fonts, Reload, search and family selection.
+5. Import an eligible `.otf` and repeat. Test empty caret, selected range, undo/redo (registration and rewrite are separate steps), malformed font, disallowed embedding, and a changed document/paragraph while selecting a file.
+6. Confirm Add Text still uses only supported standard families and does not imply custom font support.
+
+## Added regression tests (not executed)
+- `choosing_a_document_face_marks_the_draft_changed_even_with_only_a_caret`
+- `import_before_selecting_text_registers_without_rewriting_and_survives_save`
+- `a_font_pick_for_another_paragraph_does_not_change_the_open_paragraph`
+- `invalid_import_does_not_change_the_document`
+Existing `a_loaded_font_is_applied_to_the_paragraph_being_edited` was updated for the explicit paragraph target.
+
+Recommended verification: `cargo fmt --check`; `cargo clippy --locked -p pdfcraft-ui-egui --all-targets -- -D warnings`; `cargo test --locked -p pdfcraft-ui-egui`; `cargo test --locked -p pdfcraft-engine`.
